'''Li'l Yahiko''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that can be obtained by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Rurouni Kenshin Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 13.4 Update|Version 13.4]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 751
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Li'l Yahiko
|name2 = Li'l Yahiko CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Yahiko CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Li'l Yahiko is similar to Butterfly Cat, with the exception of targetting [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemies. He also trades recharge time and attack rate for Area Attack and higher range, but the 30 extra range and Area Attack aren't really enough to make him better than Fishman against Floating enemies, especially considering his recharge time is roughly 10 seconds longer.

Against Angels, he has the advantage of targeting a trait with very few usable attackers, let alone good rushers. His decent range lets him be usable against most angels, and his high speed means he can get hits on ones that still outrange him, like [[Angelic Sleipnir]]. Once unlocked though, [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]'s pure spammability and higher range make Mushroom the better choice, outside of Sleipnir.

Aside from his unique niche as an Anti-angel rusher, he is a fringe and hard to use option at best. His frankly lacking stats and elusiveness as a collab Super Rare makes him an above-average but still underwhelming collaboration unit. If one gets [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] or [[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Kalisa]], Li'l Yahiko's niche gets obliterated and relegated to labyrinth and legend quest fodder.

Regardless, keep in mind his usability when you're struggling against of floating and/or angels.

{{Job|Classification = Rusher & Nuker}}

